  "result": "The biggest gap is where the cancellation information comes from, so my first message asks about that.\n\n---\n\nI looked through the app. It builds the timetable page from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and there's no warning code yet. So the main open question is how the site would find out about a cancellation in the first place.\n\nWhen a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that news travel, and who knows first? Your answer decides most of the build: where the cancellation information comes from, who enters it, and how quickly a warning could reach the page. A nightly file can only show cancellations known the evening before, so same-day cancellations would need something else.\n\nOr if you'd rather I just dive in, say so.",
